From 6a8ff11dc06e9b7658194c87858f60024e61780e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 17:19:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06925/11362] [outer-loop] lf52: round 11 closes all three
 remaining hypotheses

Round-11 gpt-5.6-sol session closed round 10's three flagged
directions: click sequences (48 clicks across east carriers/peg, both
repeated and ordered), L6-mechanic routing (replayed real prefix
slices against L7), and non-ACTION6 controls near the east side --
none produced any state change. Found two new mechanic details along
the way (neither unlocks anything): ACTION7's immediate-undo actually
covers all of ACTION1-4, not just east-only moves; and ACTION7 right
after ACTION5 specifically cancels the armed keyhole overlay.

Independently re-verified by the outer loop: both the 615-action
prefix and the full 944-action session sequence replay cleanly from
fresh env.reset() to level=6, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED, matching
the session's own report exactly. No new level banked; frontier stays
at level 6.

After 11 rounds, every click-based interaction and every non-click
action near the east side is now exhausted. Registry entry reframes
this as a structural puzzle, not an input-discovery one, for the next
attempt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
